WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.290
Late on 13 November 1985, Nevado del Ruiz,

2
00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.090
in Colombia, erupted, hidden by a storm.

3
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.590
The town of Armero lay 45 kilometres away.

4
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.230
About 2 hours after the
eruption, the town was hit.

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.890
About 23,000 people, most
of the town, were killed.

6
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.190
Did lava really flow 45 kilometres?

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:25.710
Did an ash cloud smother the town?

8
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.350
How could a volcano reach that far?

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.250
In this mission, you'll see how silica
thickens magma and tends to make eruptions

10
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:37.410
explosive, and sort
volcanoes into three types.

11
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.470
Then you'll meet the secondary hazards,
from pyroclastic flows that typically

12
00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.010
travel faster than 80 kilometres
an hour to collapsing flanks.

13
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:51.910
Your mission: explain how a volcano 45
kilometres away killed so many people in

14
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:52.690
Armero.
